(function(E){ const x = E["exam-08"] = E["exam-08"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x08-l4"] = {"id":"x08-l4","patterns":["L4-nature","PARA-signpost","TR-plural","TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a talk on wildlife research","tr":"Listening Part 4: yaban hayatı araştırması üzerine bir konuşma","fa":"Listening Part 4: سخنرانی درباره‌ی پژوهش حیات وحش"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a long talk about wildlife research by its signposts, and complete ten notes with the exact word you hear.","tr":"Bu derste yaban hayatı araştırması üzerine uzun bir konuşmayı geçiş ifadeleriyle takip etmeyi ve on notu duyduğun kelimenin tam aynısıyla tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک سخنرانی طولانی درباره‌ی پژوهش حیات وحش را با نشانه‌های گفتاری‌اش دنبال کنی و ده یادداشت را دقیقاً با همان کلمه‌ای که می‌شنوی کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a talk on wildlife research","tr":"Listening Part 4: yaban hayatı araştırması üzerine bir konuşma","fa":"Listening Part 4: سخنرانی درباره‌ی پژوهش حیات وحش"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a long talk about wildlife research by its signposts, and complete ten notes with the exact word you hear.","tr":"Bu derste yaban hayatı araştırması üzerine uzun bir konuşmayı geçiş ifadeleriyle takip etmeyi ve on notu duyduğun kelimenin tam aynısıyla tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک سخنرانی طولانی درباره‌ی پژوهش حیات وحش را با نشانه‌های گفتاری‌اش دنبال کنی و ده یادداشت را دقیقاً با همان کلمه‌ای که می‌شنوی کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: birds of a wetland","tr":"Bu sınav: bir sulak alanın kuşları","fa":"این آزمون: پرنده‌های یک تالاب"},"intro":{"en":"Part 4 is one person speaking for about eight minutes. Animals, plants and ecosystems are the largest group of topics. Here the speaker is a researcher, so the talk moves from what the team studied to what they found and what they will do.","tr":"Part 4’te bir kişi yaklaşık sekiz dakika konuşur. Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler en büyük konu grubudur. Burada konuşan bir araştırmacı; konuşma ekibin neyi incelediğinden ne bulduğuna ve ne yapacağına doğru ilerler.","fa":"در Part 4 یک نفر حدود هشت دقیقه صحبت می‌کند. جانوران، گیاهان و زیست‌بوم‌ها بزرگ‌ترین گروه موضوع‌اند. این‌جا گوینده یک پژوهشگر است، پس صحبت از اینکه تیم چه چیزی را بررسی کرد به اینکه چه یافت و چه خواهد کرد می‌رود."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x08-l4-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L4-nature","PARA-signpost"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-nature","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A talk on research at a nature reserve","tr":"Bir doğa koruma alanındaki araştırmalar üzerine bir konuşma","fa":"سخنرانی درباره‌ی پژوهش در یک منطقه‌ی حفاظت‌شده"},"asks":{"en":"A researcher explains how a reserve was created, what the team studies about its birds, what they found, how visitors affect the wildlife and what they plan to do next. The notes follow the same order.","tr":"Bir araştırmacı bir koruma alanının nasıl oluştuğunu, ekibin kuşlarla ilgili neleri incelediğini, ne bulduklarını, ziyaretçilerin yaban hayatını nasıl etkilediğini ve sırada ne yapmayı planladıklarını anlatıyor. Notlar aynı sırayı izler.","fa":"یک پژوهشگر توضیح می‌دهد یک منطقه‌ی حفاظت‌شده چطور به وجود آمد، تیمش درباره‌ی پرنده‌ها چه چیزهایی را بررسی می‌کند، چه یافته‌اند، بازدیدکننده‌ها چه اثری روی حیات وحش دارند و برنامه‌ی بعدی‌شان چیست. یادداشت‌ها همین ترتیب را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["How the site began","How animals are counted","What they eat","Why breeding fails","Effect of visitors","Future projects"],"words":[{"a":"man-made","b":"dug out by people / created by a company","tr":"insan yapımı","fa":"ساخته‌ی دست انسان"},{"a":"count","b":"record / survey / estimate numbers","tr":"saymak","fa":"شمردن"},{"a":"by sound","b":"by ear / from the sounds they make","tr":"sesten","fa":"از روی صدا"},{"a":"diet","b":"what they eat / their main food","tr":"beslenme","fa":"رژیم غذایی"},{"a":"nest","b":"where they lay eggs and raise young","tr":"yuva","fa":"لانه"},{"a":"fail","b":"the chicks did badly / eggs were lost","tr":"başarısız olmak","fa":"شکست خوردن، از دست رفتن"},{"a":"the main cause","b":"the biggest reason / what really caused it","tr":"asıl neden","fa":"علت اصلی"},{"a":"disturb","b":"make birds take off / frighten","tr":"rahatsız etmek","fa":"مزاحم شدن، رماندن"},{"a":"volunteers","b":"local people who help for free","tr":"gönüllüler","fa":"داوطلب‌ها"},{"a":"dry out","b":"run out of water / water levels fall","tr":"kurumak","fa":"خشک شدن"},{"a":"powered by","b":"runs on / gets its energy from","tr":"... ile çalışan","fa":"با انرژیِ ... کار می‌کند"},{"a":"bare ground","b":"land with no plants on it","tr":"çıplak toprak","fa":"زمین بی‌گیاه"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"You might expect..., but in fact...\" The expected answer comes first and is wrong.","tr":"\"... bekleyebilirsiniz ama aslında...\" Beklenen cevap önce gelir ve yanlıştır.","fa":"«شاید انتظار داشته باشید...، اما در واقع...». جواب مورد انتظار اول می‌آید و غلط است."},{"en":"An old practice is replaced by a new one: \"We used to do it in spring, but now...\" The notes describe what happens now.","tr":"Eski bir uygulama yenisiyle değişir: \"Eskiden ilkbaharda yapardık ama artık...\" Notlar şimdi olanı anlatır.","fa":"یک روش قدیمی جایش را به روش تازه می‌دهد: «قبلاً بهار انجامش می‌دادیم، اما حالا...». یادداشت‌ها چیزی را می‌گویند که الان انجام می‌شود."},{"en":"Plural nouns: if you hear \"seeds\" or \"insects\", the s is part of the answer.","tr":"Çoğul isimler: \"seeds\" ya da \"insects\" duyarsan s cevabın parçasıdır.","fa":"اسم‌های جمع: اگر «seeds» یا «insects» شنیدی، s جزء جواب است."}],"example":{"lines":[["Speaker","Most visitors think the geese come here for the grass. Actually, what brings them every winter is the sugar beet left in the fields after the harvest."]],"item":"Geese · arrive in winter to feed on sugar ___","answer":"beet","why":{"en":"Grass is what visitors think. \"Actually\" gives the fact. \"sugar\" is printed, so write one word.","tr":"Ot, ziyaretçilerin sandığı şey. \"Actually\" gerçeği veriyor. \"sugar\" yazılı, tek kelime yaz.","fa":"علف چیزی است که بازدیدکننده‌ها فکر می‌کنند. «actually» واقعیت را می‌گوید. «sugar» چاپ شده، پس یک کلمه بنویس."}}},{"id":"L4-nature","ctx":["L4-nature"],"title":{"en":"Animals, plants and ecosystems","tr":"Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler","fa":"حیوان‌ها، گیاهان و زیست‌بوم‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"A lecturer explains a species, a plant or an ecosystem: where it lives, what it eats, how it behaves, what threatens it and what researchers are doing. The notes follow those headings.","tr":"Bir öğretim görevlisi bir türü, bir bitkiyi ya da bir ekosistemi anlatır: nerede yaşadığı, ne yediği, nasıl davrandığı, onu neyin tehdit ettiği ve araştırmacıların ne yaptığı. Notlar bu başlıkları izler.","fa":"یک سخنران یک گونه، یک گیاه یا یک زیست‌بوم را توضیح می‌دهد: کجا زندگی می‌کند، چه می‌خورد، چه رفتاری دارد، چه چیزی تهدیدش می‌کند و پژوهشگرها چه می‌کنند. یادداشت‌ها همین عنوان‌ها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["Habitat","Diet","Behaviour","Threats","Research methods","Conservation","Uses to humans"],"words":[{"a":"habitat","b":"where it lives / its natural home","tr":"yaşam alanı","fa":"زیستگاه"},{"a":"predators","b":"animals that hunt it","tr":"avcı hayvanlar","fa":"شکارچی‌ها"},{"a":"prey","b":"the animals it hunts","tr":"av","fa":"طعمه"},{"a":"species","b":"a type of animal or plant","tr":"tür","fa":"گونه"},{"a":"breed","b":"produce young / have babies","tr":"üremek","fa":"تولیدمثل کردن"},{"a":"migrate","b":"travel long distances every year","tr":"göç etmek","fa":"مهاجرت کردن"},{"a":"decline","b":"fall in numbers","tr":"azalma","fa":"کاهش"},{"a":"threat","b":"a danger to its survival","tr":"tehdit","fa":"تهدید"},{"a":"native","b":"it has always lived here","tr":"yerli","fa":"بومی"},{"a":"invasive","b":"brought in from elsewhere and spreading","tr":"istilacı","fa":"مهاجم"},{"a":"soil","b":"the ground plants grow in","tr":"toprak","fa":"خاک"},{"a":"track","b":"follow where it goes with a small device","tr":"izlemek","fa":"ردیابی کردن"},{"a":"conservation","b":"protecting it","tr":"koruma","fa":"حفاظت"}],"traps":[{"en":"Plurals and spelling count: insects, seeds, leaves. Write the form you hear.","tr":"Çoğul ve yazım önemlidir: insects, seeds, leaves. Duyduğun biçimi yaz.","fa":"جمع و املا مهم است: insects، seeds، leaves. همان شکلی را که می‌شنوی بنویس."},{"en":"An old belief comes first: \"it was once thought to eat fish, but in fact it mainly eats...\". Write what comes after \"in fact\".","tr":"Önce eski bir inanış gelir: \"bir zamanlar balık yediği sanılıyordu ama aslında çoğunlukla ... yiyor\". \"In fact\"ten sonra geleni yaz.","fa":"اول یک باور قدیمی می‌آید: «زمانی فکر می‌کردند ماهی می‌خورد، ولی در واقع بیشتر ... می‌خورد». چیزی را بنویس که بعد از «in fact» می‌آید."}],"example":{"lines":[["Lecturer","For a long time, people believed these birds nested on cliffs."],["Lecturer","But recent tracking shows that most of them actually nest in old trees, well away from the coast."]],"item":"Nesting site: mainly old ___   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"trees","why":{"en":"Cliffs are the old belief. \"Actually nest in old trees\": write trees, with the s.","tr":"Kayalıklar eski inanış. \"Actually nest in old trees\": trees yaz, s ile.","fa":"صخره‌ها باور قدیمی است. «Actually nest in old trees»: بنویس trees، با s."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L4-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-nature","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"One talk, ten notes, no break","tr":"Bir konuşma, on not, ara yok","fa":"یک سخنرانی، ده یادداشت، بدون مکث"},"body":{"en":"Questions 31-40 are notes under five or six headings. Write ONE WORD ONLY. You have about 45 seconds to read, and then the talk plays from start to finish without a pause. There is no second chance, so keep moving.","tr":"Soru 31-40, beş altı başlık altındaki notlardır. YALNIZCA BİR KELİME yaz. Okumak için yaklaşık 45 saniyen var, sonra konuşma baştan sona hiç durmadan çalar. İkinci şans yok, bu yüzden ilerlemeye devam et.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۴۰ یادداشت‌هایی زیر پنج شش عنوان‌اند. فقط یک کلمه بنویس. حدود ۴۵ ثانیه برای خواندن داری و بعد سخنرانی از اول تا آخر بدون مکث پخش می‌شود. فرصت دوباره‌ای نیست، پس جلو برو."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the headings first: they are the map of the talk.","tr":"Önce başlıkları oku: konuşmanın haritası onlardır.","fa":"اول عنوان‌ها را بخوان: نقشه‌ی سخنرانی‌اند."},{"en":"Listen for signposts that move you on: \"Let me start with\", \"Moving on to\", \"I’d like to turn now to\", \"Finally\".","tr":"Seni ilerleten geçiş ifadelerine kulak ver: \"Let me start with\", \"Moving on to\", \"I’d like to turn now to\", \"Finally\".","fa":"به نشانه‌هایی گوش بده که تو را جلو می‌برند: «Let me start with»، «Moving on to»، «I’d like to turn now to»، «Finally»."},{"en":"Read the words before and after each gap: the speaker will say them in other words.","tr":"Her boşluğun önündeki ve arkasındaki kelimeleri oku: konuşan onları başka kelimelerle söyleyecek.","fa":"کلمه‌های قبل و بعد از هر جای خالی را بخوان: گوینده آن‌ها را با کلمه‌های دیگری می‌گوید."},{"en":"Write the word exactly as you hear it, with any plural s, and check the spelling at the end.","tr":"Kelimeyi duyduğun gibi, varsa çoğul s ile yaz ve sonda yazımı kontrol et.","fa":"کلمه را دقیقاً همان‌طور که می‌شنوی بنویس، با s جمع اگر هست، و آخر کار املا را چک کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The expected answer comes first","tr":"Beklenen cevap önce gelir","fa":"جواب مورد انتظار اول می‌آید"},"body":{"en":"Lecturers like to correct common beliefs. \"Most people blamed X... but the cameras showed Y.\" When you hear \"you might expect\", \"most people think\" or \"in fact\", the answer is usually the second idea.","tr":"Konuşmacılar yaygın inanışları düzeltmeyi sever. \"Çoğu kişi X’i suçladı... ama kameralar Y’yi gösterdi.\" \"you might expect\", \"most people think\" ya da \"in fact\" duyduğunda cevap genelde ikinci fikirdir.","fa":"سخنران‌ها دوست دارند باورهای رایج را اصلاح کنند. «بیشتر مردم X را مقصر می‌دانستند... اما دوربین‌ها Y را نشان دادند». وقتی «you might expect»، «most people think» یا «in fact» می‌شنوی، جواب معمولاً ایده‌ی دوم است."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One note, step by step","tr":"Bir not, adım adım","fa":"یک یادداشت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","item":"Owls · young owls are fed mainly on ___","lines":[["Speaker","People picture owls catching mice, and they do. But when we looked at the pellets, most of the food brought to the young turned out to be beetles."]],"answer":"beetles","walk":[{"en":"The gap needs a kind of food, and \"young owls\" tells you which sentence to wait for.","tr":"Boşluk bir yiyecek türü istiyor; \"young owls\" hangi cümleyi beklemen gerektiğini söylüyor.","fa":"جای خالی نوعی غذا می‌خواهد و «young owls» می‌گوید منتظر کدام جمله باشی."},{"en":"\"Mice\" is what people picture; \"but\" and \"turned out to be\" bring the fact.","tr":"\"Mice\" insanların hayal ettiği; \"but\" ve \"turned out to be\" gerçeği getiriyor.","fa":"«mice» تصویری است که مردم دارند؛ «but» و «turned out to be» واقعیت را می‌آورند."},{"en":"Write beetles, with the plural s you hear.","tr":"Duyduğun çoğul s ile beetles yaz.","fa":"beetles را با همان s جمعی که می‌شنوی بنویس."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Notes: \"Fish counted using ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". You hear: \"We used to use nets, but now we count them with underwater cameras.\" What do you write?","options":["nets","cameras","underwater cameras"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Nets were the old method. Cameras is one word; \"underwater cameras\" is two.","tr":"Ağlar eski yöntemdi. Cameras tek kelime; \"underwater cameras\" iki kelime.","fa":"تور روش قدیمی بود. cameras یک کلمه است؛ «underwater cameras» دو کلمه."}},"remember":{"en":"Use the headings as a map, follow the signposts, and write the exact word in its plural or singular form.","tr":"Başlıkları harita gibi kullan, geçiş ifadelerini takip et ve kelimeyi tam olarak, tekil ya da çoğul biçimiyle yaz.","fa":"عنوان‌ها را مثل نقشه به کار ببر، نشانه‌ها را دنبال کن و کلمه را دقیقاً با شکل مفرد یا جمعش بنویس."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x08-l4-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-l4"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 4","title":{"en":"Research at Fenmoor wetland reserve","tr":"Fenmoor sulak alanında araştırma","fa":"پژوهش در تالاب فن‌مور"},"timed":8,"ctx":["L4-nature"],"script":[{"who":"Speaker","line":"Good evening, everyone, and thank you for coming. I've been working at Fenmoor wetland reserve for six years now, and tonight I'd like to give you an idea of the research we do there, what we've learned, and what we're planning next."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"Let me start with the reserve itself. People often assume it's an ancient marsh that has simply been left alone. In fact, almost the whole site was dug out for gravel in the nineteen-sixties and seventies. When the quarrying stopped, the pits filled with water, and the company planted reeds around the edges. So it's really a man-made landscape, even though it looks completely wild today."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"Our main research focus is the bittern, a shy brown heron that lives deep in the reed beds. You hardly ever see one, so how do we know how many there are? The answer is that we don't count the birds by sight at all. In spring the males make a very deep, booming sound, and each male's sound is slightly different. So our team goes out before dawn and records them, and we count the males by listening to their calls. When I started, there were three. Last spring we counted eleven."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"Now, reeds don't look after themselves. If you leave a reed bed for too long, dead stems build up, the ground gets drier, and eventually bushes and trees take over. So every year we cut sections of reed on a rotation. We used to do this in the autumn, but we found that it disturbed birds that were still feeding there, so now all the cutting is done in winter, when the ground is frozen and the machines don't damage it."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"We've also been studying what bitterns eat. You might expect frogs to be the main item, and they do eat some. But when we analysed the remains around their feeding areas, it turned out that by far the most important food was eels. That's significant, because eel numbers have fallen across Europe, so protecting them in our ditches helps the bitterns too."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"Moving on to the wet grassland at the southern end of the reserve. This is where wading birds such as lapwings nest on the ground. For several years their chicks did very badly, and we wanted to know why. Most people blamed predators, and some nests are taken, of course. But the cameras we put on the nests told a different story. The biggest cause of failure was flooding after heavy rain, because the nests were in the lowest, wettest parts of the field."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"To understand this better, we placed small sensors inside a sample of nests. These record the temperature every few minutes, so we can see exactly when a parent leaves the eggs and how long they stay cold. It's a cheap method, and it's given us a very detailed picture of how the birds behave during bad weather."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"I'd like to turn now to visitors. Fenmoor gets about sixty thousand visitors a year, and we want people to enjoy it, but we also need to understand how they affect the birds. So for a year we watched how birds reacted to people on the paths. Walkers on their own, or in small groups, caused surprisingly little disturbance. The birds soon learned that they stayed on the path. What made birds take off, again and again, was dogs, especially dogs running off the lead along the water's edge."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"As a result, dogs must now be kept on a lead everywhere on the reserve, and we've closed one short path during the nesting season. Visitor numbers haven't fallen at all, and the number of birds feeding near that path has almost doubled."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"A lot of this work depends on volunteers. Every month, about forty local people help us count the birds on the main lake. In the past they wrote everything on paper forms, and it took us weeks to type them up. Now they enter their counts straight into an app on their phones, so the results are on our computers the same afternoon."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"Finally, what about the future? The biggest risk for a wetland is, quite simply, running out of water. Our summers are getting hotter and drier, and in two of the last five years parts of the reserve dried out completely. So we're installing pumps that will move water from the deepest pit into the reed beds when levels fall. They'll be powered by solar panels, so they won't add to our running costs."},{"who":"Speaker","line":"And our last project is for the terns, small seabirds that come inland to nest. They need bare ground surrounded by water, where foxes can't reach them. So this winter we'll be building a group of floating islands on the main lake, covered in gravel. If they work, we hope to have our first tern nests next summer. Thank you. I'm happy to take questions."}],"notes":{"title":"Research at Fenmoor wetland reserve","headings":["The site","Bitterns","Wading birds","Visitors","Volunteers","Future projects"],"extra":["Visitors · dogs must now be kept on a lead","Future projects · first tern nests hoped for next summer"]},"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 31-40. Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","qtype":"note","questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The site · was dug out for ___ in the 1960s and 1970s","accept":["gravel"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the whole site was dug out for gravel","why":{"en":"It is not an ancient marsh: \"the whole site was dug out for gravel\".","tr":"Eski bir bataklık değil: \"bütün alan çakıl için kazıldı\".","fa":"یک باتلاق قدیمی نیست: «کل محوطه برای شن‌وماسه کنده شد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-ruledout"]},{"n":32,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Bitterns · males are counted by listening to their ___","accept":["calls"],"limit":1,"evidence":"listening to their calls","why":{"en":"\"We count the males by listening to their calls.\" Write the plural.","tr":"\"Erkekleri seslerini dinleyerek sayıyoruz.\" Çoğul yaz.","fa":"«نرها را با گوش دادن به صدایشان می‌شماریم». جمع بنویس."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":33,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Bitterns · reeds are cut every year in ___","accept":["winter"],"limit":1,"evidence":"now all the cutting is done in winter","why":{"en":"Autumn was the old practice. \"Now all the cutting is done in winter.\"","tr":"Sonbahar eski uygulamaydı. \"Artık bütün kesim kışın yapılıyor.\"","fa":"پاییز روش قدیمی بود. «حالا همه‌ی بریدن‌ها در زمستان انجام می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-selfcorrect"]},{"n":34,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Bitterns · their most important food is ___","accept":["eels"],"limit":1,"evidence":"by far the most important food was eels","why":{"en":"Frogs are what \"you might expect\". The remains showed eels. Plural.","tr":"Kurbağalar \"bekleyebileceğiniz\" şey. Kalıntılar yılan balığını gösterdi. Çoğul.","fa":"قورباغه چیزی است که «شاید انتظار داشته باشید». بقایا مارماهی را نشان داد. جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-ruledout"]},{"n":35,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Wading birds · most nests failed because of flooding after heavy ___","accept":["rain"],"limit":1,"evidence":"flooding after heavy rain","why":{"en":"Predators are what \"most people blamed\". The cameras showed flooding after heavy rain.","tr":"\"Çoğu kişinin suçladığı\" yırtıcılar. Kameralar şiddetli yağmurdan sonraki su baskınını gösterdi.","fa":"شکارچی‌ها چیزی‌اند که «بیشتر مردم مقصر می‌دانستند». دوربین‌ها آب‌گرفتگی بعد از باران شدید را نشان دادند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Wading birds · sensors inside nests record the ___","accept":["temperature"],"limit":1,"evidence":"These record the temperature every few minutes","why":{"en":"\"These record the temperature every few minutes.\"","tr":"\"Bunlar birkaç dakikada bir sıcaklığı kaydediyor.\"","fa":"«این‌ها هر چند دقیقه یک بار دما را ثبت می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Visitors · birds were disturbed most by ___","accept":["dogs"],"limit":1,"evidence":"was dogs, especially dogs running off the lead","why":{"en":"Walkers caused \"surprisingly little disturbance\". What made birds take off was dogs. Plural.","tr":"Yürüyüşçüler \"şaşırtıcı derecede az rahatsızlık\" verdi. Kuşları uçuran köpeklerdi. Çoğul.","fa":"پیاده‌ها «به‌طرز عجیبی مزاحمت کمی» داشتند. چیزی که پرنده‌ها را می‌پراند سگ‌ها بودند. جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-ruledout"]},{"n":38,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Volunteers · monthly counts are now entered into an ___","accept":["app"],"limit":1,"evidence":"straight into an app on their phones","why":{"en":"Paper forms were the old way. Now they use \"an app on their phones\".","tr":"Kâğıt formlar eski yöntemdi. Artık \"telefonlarındaki bir uygulamayı\" kullanıyorlar.","fa":"فرم کاغذی روش قدیمی بود. حالا از «یک اپ روی گوشی‌شان» استفاده می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Future projects · water pumps powered by ___ panels","accept":["solar"],"limit":1,"evidence":"powered by solar panels","why":{"en":"\"panels\" is printed; write one word: solar.","tr":"\"panels\" yazılı; tek kelime yaz: solar.","fa":"«panels» چاپ شده؛ یک کلمه بنویس: solar."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":40,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Future projects · floating ___ on the main lake for terns","accept":["islands"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a group of floating islands on the main lake","why":{"en":"\"Floating\" is printed. Write islands, with the s.","tr":"\"Floating\" yazılı. s ile islands yaz.","fa":"«floating» چاپ شده. islands را با s بنویس."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-limit"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Speaker":{"accent":"Australian","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bf_isabella","fallback":true,"note":"Australian wanted; no free Australian voice yet"},"role":"Researcher giving a talk"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 4. You will hear a talk about research at a wetland reserve. First, you have some time to look at Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"pause","seconds":45,"note":"reading time, Questions 31-40"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"sfx","note":"small hall: slight reverb; 1.5 s pause between paragraphs"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":11},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 4. You now have two minutes to check your answers.","after":120}]},"id":"c-x08-l4-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-l4"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"A speaker says the land was \"man-made\". This means...","options":["people created it","it is very old","men work there"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Man-made = made by people, not by nature.","tr":"Man-made = doğa değil, insanlar tarafından yapılmış.","fa":"man-made یعنی ساخته‌ی دست انسان، نه طبیعت."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"Notes: \"main cause of failure: ___\". Which phrase in a talk leads you to it?","options":["some people blamed","we also looked at","the biggest reason was"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"The biggest reason\" = the main cause. \"Some people blamed\" introduces a distractor.","tr":"\"The biggest reason\" = ana neden. \"Some people blamed\" çeldiriciyi getirir.","fa":"«the biggest reason» یعنی علت اصلی. «some people blamed» گزینه‌ی انحرافی را می‌آورد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"You hear \"I’d like to turn now to visitors.\" What should you do?","options":["Write \"visitors\" in the next gap","Move your eyes to the Visitors heading","Go back and check the earlier gaps"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A signpost tells you the talk has reached the next heading.","tr":"Geçiş ifadesi konuşmanın sonraki başlığa geldiğini söyler.","fa":"نشانه می‌گوید سخنرانی به عنوان بعدی رسیده."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Notes: \"nests are built on ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". You hear \"they always nest on small islands\". What do you write?","options":["islands","island","small islands"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Copy the plural you hear; \"small islands\" is two words.","tr":"Duyduğun çoğulu yaz; \"small islands\" iki kelime.","fa":"همان جمعی را که می‌شنوی بنویس؛ «small islands» دو کلمه است."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"Most people think the birds leave because of the cold. In fact, it’s the lack of food.\" Notes: \"birds leave because of a lack of ___\". What do you write?","options":["cold","people","food"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Most people think\" brings the distractor (cold); \"in fact\" brings the answer.","tr":"\"Most people think\" çeldiriciyi (soğuk) getiriyor; \"in fact\" cevabı getiriyor.","fa":"«most people think» گزینه‌ی انحرافی (سرما) را می‌آورد؛ «in fact» جواب را."}}],"id":"c-x08-l4-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-l4"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
